8b:["$","p","78",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"กระทำกิจการใด ๆ ที่เกี่ยวข้องกับผลประโยชน์ของส่วนรวมได้  ท้ายที่สุด เพื่อให้ระเบียบฉบับนี้สามารถรองรับความหลากหลายและมีความเป็นสากล จึงได้กำหนดให้จัดทำร่างระเบียบฉบับนี้ขึ้นเป็นทั้งภาษาไทยและภาษาอังกฤษ โดยระบุเงื่อนไขให้ยึดถือเอาข้อความตามระเบียบฉบับภาษาไทยเป็นฉบับที่ใช้บังคับหลักหากมีความขัดแย้งหรือมีปัญหาในการตีความ  ด้วยเหตุผลและความจำเป็นในการปรับปรุงกลไกการทำงานดังกล่าวข้างต้น จึงสมควรให้มีการตราระเบียบฉบับนี้ขึ้น"}]]]}]
13c:T7e6,Shwe Tint Tal, Honourable Chair, distinguished members of the Student Council, My name is Coleen, from the Renew TPC party. I rise to propose the motion to repeal the Student Activity Regulations of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan Campus, B.E. 2565 (2022), regarding the operations and meetings of the Student Council, and to adopt the new draft regulations of B.E. 2569 (2026) as a complete replacement. For a period of time, this Student Council has operated under the 2022 regulations. However, it has become evident that the context of student activities, the formats of meetings, as well as the internal administrative structure of the Council have significantly changed. As a result, the provisions, procedures, and working mechanisms prescribed in the existing regulations have encountered limitations. They are no longer fully applicable to the current situation, and in certain aspects, they have become obstacles to the efficiency and flexibility of Council members and various committees in performing their duties. Therefore, in order to ensure that the operations and meetings of the Student Council are conducted efficiently, with mechanisms that are transparent and accountable, and capable of genuinely responding to the protection of students' rights, it is deemed appropriate to draft a new set of regulations to replace the existing one in its entirety. The proposed 2026 regulations aim to address existing shortcomings and to organize powers and responsibilities with greater clarity and completeness. This motion is submitted under the authority of the existing regulations, calling upon this Council to consider repealing the 2022 regulations and enacting the 2026 regulations as a complete replacement. In doing so, the administrative mechanisms, meeting procedures, and internal coordination of the Student Council will become more flexible, transparent, and aligned with the current context of student activities. Therefore, I respectfully urge this Council to consider and approve this motion.8c:["$","p","79",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"$13c"}]]]}]
